{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 8f7135046a767c0d303c1b4d9c77622f61098d92 on builder/u2-upgrade-archive-20261117, all 9 artifacts, for request 0a6aef6e under my promise a327149b. The implementation is U2 (request 7e9cad2a, promise a0595352). The reporting artifact is the U2 note.\n\nThe head adds two commits to origin main 7cb207e1, so the merge tree equals the head's tree, ec8899f0.\n\n## What I read\n\n- The note first, then the source diff of `archive-packages.ts`, `archive.ts`, `archive-proof.ts` and `archive-driver.ts`.\n- In place. `installed` now compares the proof's semantic identifier, root definition, scope and seed definition with the birth values, and no longer compares release and presentation. The birth-release trust check before the proof goes. `add` still checks `APPLICATION_TRUST` for the item's current release, so an untrusted current release still stops the archive as revoked.\n- Replace. `storedApplicationArchiveProof` proves a `replaced` item from the slots it held when it ended and wraps the bytes as `{ replaced }`. Only the archive reads this proof: `object.ts:873` serves it and `archive-packages.ts:105` calls it. No admission or trust path reads it. `prepare` answers `{ final: \"application-replaced\" }` only for the archived scope itself. A replay source or Directory candidate that names a replaced item keeps its policies.\n- The driver. `final` sets no stop at once. `#final` ends a pass only when it is confirmed with `next === null`, which means the append reached the scope's head. The caught-up branch ends the archive after its existing check that the head has not moved. Both use the pass's single `prepareHalt`, which writes the terminal and the wake index `{ pending: false, stopped: true, next: null }`.\n\n## Wake rate\n\nI read every path that writes the archive wake index or the alarm:\n\n- `ArchiveRows.signal` (`archive-row.ts:529`) is the only caller path from `committed(sealed)`, both from a sealed commit and from activation (`archive-driver.ts:134-136`). It returns at once when the wake index says `stopped`, so neither a new entry nor a constructor activation restarts a stopped archive.\n- `clearWake` (`archive-row.ts:517`) runs only on the idle branch. The `final` branch returns before it, so it cannot clear the stopped flag.\n- `prepareHalt` writes the terminal with `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` and works only once per pass.\n- `committed` arms `#later(0)` as its fallback only when `signal` throws. The stopped return does not throw.\n- The Durable Object alarm itself is set only in `object.ts:226` and `worker.ts:178`, from `wake()`. U2 changes neither.\n\nThe wake floor of an idle or stopped scope stays at zero archive wakes an hour. In place, U2 removes the AR-1 retry that a release mismatch started: up to about 42 requests in the first hour, then about 7 an hour for ever. A replaced scope that is caught up costs one pass, about 7 requests, once. One that is not caught up makes the passes that publish its backlog, each continuing at once as any append does, then stops. A replaced scope that keeps taking acts makes passes at most at its own commit rate until a pass reaches the head. AD-1 (7ebe8ec3) closes that by refusing new acts in a replaced scope. The per-room rate is bounded in every case.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- The gate. END bcae71b1 passed at this head. The first line of `artroom-evidence/2026-11-17-u2-gate-2/gate.txt` names this head with 0 changed files, and the log ends \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\". The builder stopped the earlier gate at c9be116c because the ruling moved the head (c77db579).\n- The reds. `artroom-evidence/2026-11-17-u2-red/` holds `1.txt`, `1b.txt`, `2.txt`, `2b.txt`, `2c.txt` and `2d.txt`. Their SHA-256 values equal the six in the note's table.\n- Scope. The 9 artifacts name the head and equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 7cb207e1 8f713504`. The four moved seals match the four source files.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 2 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n- The ruling. The note states the stop limit of ruling 2b1bae37 in one sentence. It answers its question with code evidence (`act-admission.ts:87-100`), and it records facts (1) and (2) as written.\n\nArchitecture: sound. `final` reuses the existing terminal write and wake index, so the stop needs no new state.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. Proving a replaced item reaches only the archive, and the archive still checks trust on the current release. The gap where a replaced scope still admits acts belongs to AD-1, and the note names it.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nRuling 8f26aa9b deploys U1 and U2 together. This approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:237bd6a2645dbf6ff0068084fb071cdc9014cf85","binding":"assigned","head":"8f7135046a767c0d303c1b4d9c77622f61098d92","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a327149ba9e5b5b6a1881d4033a5274a5a164a23\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a0595352abd4bfc2cdd953d3a129f7707713f4b5\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a327149ba9e5b5b6a1881d4033a5274a5a164a23","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}